Reason:
When the preparation of a command fails, the code detaches the failed request from the original list but does not properly update the pointers to maintain the integrity of the list. This results in the original list still pointing to the failed request, leading to attempts to submit an unprepared command and orphaning subsequent requests.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
rq_list_move(rqlist, &requeue_list, req, prev);
req = prev;
